{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>You</b> — Just as he mentioned His throne in heaven, he mentioned His throne on earth in the place of Zion, in the manner of \"the place of our sanctuary.\" So you have promised us that Zion shall stand forever, in the dwelling of Your glory there. And he said: \"will arise\" opposite \"sit,\" for this will be after rising to do battle with His enemies." "<b>To grant favor</b> — A noun [infinitive construct], and it has a segol, which is a minor pataḥ under a major one, like פן אכלך (Lamentations 4:10); both are light [beged-kefet letters] without a dagesh."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 102, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:50.313438203Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}